      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, or shock. An overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilation that is hard to reverse. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change this.\n\nThere are two other issues:\n- **Prescriber:** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If you're not a clinician, the order should go through the patient's clinical team.\n- **Possible typo:** The intended dose may have been 5 mg, which is the usual starting dose, or 10 mg.\n\nIf the treating clinician confirms a dose within the standard range of 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, I can enter it. If they really intend a dose above the maximum, they should enter it themselves and document why. Pharmacy review would also be needed."
      }
