       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problems are the same as before.\n\n- **Dose:** 50 mg is five times the 10 mg daily maximum, and nothing in the patient's profile justifies it. It could cause serious harm.\n- **Prescriber:** The confirmation has to come from the licensed clinician responsible for this patient. It can't come from an administrator.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- The treating physician or another authorized prescriber can enter the order themselves. They would need to document the clinical rationale and get pharmacy review.\n- If a lower dose was intended, tell me and I'll enter it. A dose of 5 mg or 10 mg once daily would be within range.\n- If the patient needs stronger blood pressure control, the clinical team can add another agent or titrate safely.\n\nIf you tell me the clinician's name and the intended dose, I can help with the next step."
